From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0794: warm-up at start of the host allocations the first frames of a scene make (shared memory and scaled resolve tile heaps, host render targets), from the keys of earlier runs, with a budget; a seed key file for a first run

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (hitch work of 2026-11-27, scratch/hitch2/DESIGN.md; extends 0790 and 0793)
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: The first 3D frame of a run commits about 35 MiB of new private memory and the first 1080p scene about 70-80 MiB (the host's
  mcla_pf_probe_ms bursts of runs b-p5..b-p8), in frames of 66-73 ms and 82-159 ms. The shared memory is a 512 MB tiled buffer whose 4 MB
  tile heaps are made on the first request of each part of the guest's memory (D3D12SharedMemory::AllocateSparseHostGpuMemoryRange: a
  CreateHeap, a wait for the submission thread, UpdateTileMappings; every resolve's RequestRange does it for its destination, also when
  nothing is uploaded). The 4 MB windows the logs name (the destinations of resolves and direct texture loads) are the same in every run:
  8 in the first engine frame (32 MiB; the bursts commit 33.6-35.5) and 11 in the first 1080p frame (44 MiB; the bursts of that frame
  commit 68-81, 14-28k page faults a frame; the rest is by arithmetic the host render targets, which are zeroed committed resources);
  at a draw resolution scale above 1 the scaled resolve buffer's 16 MB tile heaps are made the same way. This keeps the keys of what is made, in
  0790's file: kind 5 a host render target (RenderTargetKey::key, appended by D3D12RenderTargetCache::CreateRenderTarget), 6 a shared
  memory tile heap window (granularity log2 << 24 | index, by AllocateSparseHostGpuMemoryRange), 7 a scaled resolve tile heap (draw scale
  x << 28 | y << 24 | heap index, by EnsureScaledResolveMemoryCommitted). D3D12CommandProcessor::WarmUpHostAllocations, called by
  InitializeShaderStorage after the pipelines, makes the ones this run's layout can ask for, in the order the earlier run needed them
  in, within d3d12_warmup_mib (0 = 1024 MiB times the draw resolution scale's area, and never more than a quarter of the free video
  memory the OS reports): the shared memory windows first (neighbours in one heap, up to 8 windows each), then the scaled resolve
  heaps, then the render targets (new RenderTargetCache::PrecreateRenderTarget: a failure is not remembered, so the draw that needs the
  render target tries itself, and its last use is the time of the warm-up, so render_target_trim_seconds treats it as made at start).
  It logs '[warm-up] N host allocations (M MiB) made in X ms from the key file: ...' with the time and size of each kind and what it
  left to the first use (over the budget, not for this layout, failed). The tile heaps still made while the game runs are logged with
  what they cost (the first 64: 'Shared memory: a 4 MB tile heap for the guest memory at 0x... made while the game runs: heap N us,
  wait for the submission thread and tile mapping M us'; the same for the scaled resolve heaps), which settles how much of a hitch they
  are. cvars: d3d12_warmup (true), d3d12_warmup_mib (0), d3d12_warmup_seed (default empty: the path of a key file made on the same kind
  of GPU, which a run with no key file of its own starts from, so a first run makes at start what that run made; the key files hold
  only numbers). The first run on a cache, with no seed, behaves as before. Left lazy on purpose: textures (their keys are guest
  addresses; they are placed in the 256 MB heap the first texture makes), the upload buffer pool pages, descriptor heaps and the EDRAM
  buffer (made at start already), readback buffers, HDR / temporal AA / frame generation resources (features off). The key file
  context (its header) is unchanged, so an existing file stays valid.
  Needs 0790, 0791, 0792, 0760 and 0793.
  Measured (2026-11-27, RTX 4060 Laptop, runs h2-*): the key file of a long drive holds 94 shared memory windows (376 MiB) and 35 host
  render targets (236 MiB) at 1080p, not the 19 windows of the first estimate, so the default budget is 1024 MiB times the draw
  scale's area (a 256 MiB budget made 51 of 125 objects and left 74 to the first use: worst front-end frame 117 ms). At 1080p it makes
  129 objects (612 MiB) in 31-35 ms (windows 16-20 ms, render targets 15 ms); at 2000p 154 objects (1723 MiB, the cap of a quarter of the
  free video memory) in 67 ms. Worst 1080p front-end frame, median of 3: 109.5 ms without the warm-up (0793 alone), 81 ms with it
  (53-87); the run-time tile heap lines go from 64+ to 0. Process video memory at 1080p 1.21 GB against 1.09 GB, at 2000p 3.56 GB against
  2.88 GB of a 7.19 GB budget. Not removed: the first engine frame (60-80 ms) and the loading frame (42-57 ms) are not allocations; what
  is left of the front-end frame is the first creation and touch of about 30 to 80 upload buffer pages (2 MiB each) and the scene's
  600 textures (see docs/LEARNINGS NATIVE-S).
Bucket: REDO

0794-host-allocation-warm-up.patch (mcla-x86 native stream, T0/T2).

---
diff --git a/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.h b/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.h
--- a/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.h
+++ b/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.h
@@ -70,6 +70,17 @@ class D3D12CommandProcessor : public CommandProcessor {
   std::string ShaderStorageReport(bool shutdown) override;
   void FlushShaderStorage(uint32_t timeout_ms) override;  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0792)
 
+  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0794): the host allocations that the first frames of a scene make on first use (the shared
+  // memory's and the scaled resolve buffer's tile heaps, the host render targets) are made at start, from the keys of
+  // the earlier runs (<title>.rtv.d3d12.xrtp, kinds 5 to 7), up to a budget; called by InitializeShaderStorage after the
+  // pipelines. RecordWarmupKey is what the shared memory and the texture cache keep their keys with.
+  void RecordWarmupKey(uint32_t kind, uint32_t key) {
+    if (render_target_cache_) {
+      render_target_cache_->RecordWarmupKey(kind, key);
+    }
+  }
+  void WarmUpHostAllocations();
+
   ui::d3d12::D3D12Provider& GetD3D12Provider() const {
     return *static_cast<ui::d3d12::D3D12Provider*>(graphics_system_->provider());
   }
diff --git a/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/render_target_cache.h b/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/render_target_cache.h
--- a/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/render_target_cache.h
+++ b/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/render_target_cache.h
@@ -73,6 +73,23 @@ class D3D12RenderTargetCache final : public RenderTargetCache {
   void InitializeRuntimePipelineStorage(const std::filesystem::path& cache_root,
                                         uint32_t title_id);
 
+  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0794): the host allocations made on first use, kept in the same file (the keys of kinds 5 to
+  // 7), for D3D12CommandProcessor::WarmUpHostAllocations to make at start. The key of a render target is its
+  // RenderTargetKey::key, of a shared memory tile heap (kWarmupKindSharedMemoryWindow) the granularity's log2 << 24 |
+  // its index, of a scaled resolve tile heap the draw resolution scale x << 28 | y << 24 | the heap index.
+  static constexpr uint32_t kWarmupKindRenderTarget = 5;
+  static constexpr uint32_t kWarmupKindSharedMemoryWindow = 6;
+  static constexpr uint32_t kWarmupKindScaledResolveHeap = 7;
+  // For the shared memory and the texture cache, which make the other two kinds, through the command processor.
+  void RecordWarmupKey(uint32_t kind, uint32_t key) { RecordRuntimePipelineKey(kind, key); }
+  // The records of the three kinds in the file, in the order the earlier runs made them in (and so needed them in);
+  // moves them out.
+  std::vector<uint64_t> TakeWarmupRecords() { return std::move(warmup_records_); }
+  // The host memory the render target of the key takes, 0 if it is not one this cache can make.
+  uint64_t EstimateWarmupRenderTargetBytes(uint32_t key_value) const;
+  // Makes the render target of the key now (see RenderTargetCache::PrecreateRenderTarget).
+  bool WarmUpRenderTarget(uint32_t key_value, uint64_t& host_memory_bytes_out);
+
   void CompletedSubmissionUpdated();
   void BeginSubmission();
 
@@ -838,8 +855,14 @@ class D3D12RenderTargetCache final : public RenderTargetCache {
     // A record made with another draw resolution scale stays in the file and isn't made at another scale.
     kRuntimePipelineKeyDirectResolveDual = 3,
     kRuntimePipelineKeyDirectResolveStretch = 4,
-    kRuntimePipelineKeyLast = kRuntimePipelineKeyDirectResolveStretch,
+    // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0794): the host allocations (see RecordWarmupKey), not pipelines.
+    kRuntimePipelineKeyRenderTarget = kWarmupKindRenderTarget,
+    kRuntimePipelineKeySharedMemoryWindow = kWarmupKindSharedMemoryWindow,
+    kRuntimePipelineKeyScaledResolveHeap = kWarmupKindScaledResolveHeap,
+    kRuntimePipelineKeyLast = kRuntimePipelineKeyScaledResolveHeap,
   };
+  // The records of kinds 5 to 7 read from the file, until TakeWarmupRecords.
+  std::vector<uint64_t> warmup_records_;
   // Appends the key to the file (and flushes: a few dozen records a run, and the process ends with _Exit) unless it
   // is already there or the keys are being made from the file.
   void RecordRuntimePipelineKey(uint32_t kind, uint32_t key);
diff --git a/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/shared_memory.h b/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/shared_memory.h
--- a/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/shared_memory.h
+++ b/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/shared_memory.h
@@ -122,6 +122,14 @@ class D3D12SharedMemory : public SharedMemory {
   void WriteUintPow2UAVDescriptor(D3D12_CPU_DESCRIPTOR_HANDLE handle,
                                   uint32_t element_size_bytes_pow2);
 
+  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0794): the tile heaps of the sparse shared memory are made on the first request of each 4 MB
+  // of the guest's memory (the textures a resolve writes, the vertex data uploaded): 19 of them in the first frames of
+  // the game's front end, 8 to 11 of them in each of the first frame and the first 1080p frame, each a CreateHeap, a
+  // wait for the submission thread and a tile mapping. UINT32_MAX when the memory isn't sparse.
+  uint32_t GetSparseAllocationGranularityLog2() const { return host_gpu_memory_sparse_granularity_log2(); }
+  // Makes the heaps behind the range now, at start (EnsureRangeAllocated; not logged as a run-time creation).
+  bool WarmUpHostGpuMemory(uint32_t start, uint32_t length);
+
  protected:
   bool AllocateSparseHostGpuMemoryRange(uint32_t offset_allocations,
                                         uint32_t length_allocations) override;
@@ -131,6 +139,11 @@ class D3D12SharedMemory : public SharedMemory {
  private:
   D3D12CommandProcessor& command_processor_;
 
+  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0794): inside WarmUpHostGpuMemory; the heaps made then are not logged one by one.
+  bool warming_up_ = false;
+  // Run-time tile heaps logged so far (the first few are, with what they cost).
+  uint32_t runtime_heaps_logged_ = 0;
+
   // The 512 MB tiled buffer.
   ID3D12Resource* buffer_ = nullptr;
   D3D12_GPU_VIRTUAL_ADDRESS buffer_gpu_address_ = 0;
diff --git a/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/texture_cache.h b/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/texture_cache.h
--- a/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/texture_cache.h
+++ b/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/texture_cache.h
@@ -139,6 +139,11 @@ class D3D12TextureCache final : public TextureCache {
   // Ensures the tiles backing the range in the buffers are allocated.
   bool EnsureScaledResolveMemoryCommitted(uint32_t start_unscaled, uint32_t length_unscaled,
                                           uint32_t length_scaled_alignment_log2 = 0) override;
+  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0794): at a draw resolution scale above 1 the tile heaps of the scaled resolve buffer (16 MB
+  // each, 4 times the shared memory's at 2x2) are made on the first resolve or load of each part of it, like the shared
+  // memory's. Makes the heap of the index now, at start (the key of an earlier run); not logged as a run-time creation.
+  bool WarmUpScaledResolveHeap(uint32_t heap_index);
+  static constexpr uint64_t GetScaledResolveHeapBytes() { return uint64_t(1) << kScaledResolveHeapSizeLog2; }
   // Makes the specified range of up to 1-2 GB currently accessible on the GPU.
   // One draw call can access only at most one range - the same memory is
   // accessible through different buffers based on the range needed, so aliasing
@@ -883,6 +888,9 @@ class D3D12TextureCache final : public TextureCache {
   std::vector<Microsoft::WRL::ComPtr<ID3D12Heap>> scaled_resolve_heaps_;
   // Number of currently resident portions of the tiled buffer, for profiling.
   uint32_t scaled_resolve_heap_count_ = 0;
+  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0794): inside WarmUpScaledResolveHeap; and how many run-time heaps are logged so far.
+  bool warming_up_scaled_resolve_ = false;
+  uint32_t runtime_scaled_resolve_heaps_logged_ = 0;
   // Current scaled resolve state.
   // For aliasing barrier placement, last owning buffer index for each of 1 GB.
   size_t scaled_resolve_1gb_buffer_indices_[(uint64_t(SharedMemory::kBufferSize) *
diff --git a/include/rex/graphics/pipeline/render_target/cache.h b/include/rex/graphics/pipeline/render_target/cache.h
--- a/include/rex/graphics/pipeline/render_target/cache.h
+++ b/include/rex/graphics/pipeline/render_target/cache.h
@@ -575,6 +575,13 @@ class RenderTargetCache {
 
   virtual RenderTarget* CreateRenderTarget(RenderTargetKey key) = 0;
 
+  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0794): makes the host render target of the key now unless it exists (the key of an earlier
+  // run, at start, so the first frame that draws to it doesn't make it) on the host render targets path. Returns
+  // whether it exists after the call, and how much host memory a new one takes in host_memory_bytes_out (0 if it
+  // existed). Unlike GetOrCreateRenderTarget, a failure isn't remembered: the draw that needs the render target
+  // tries to make it itself. Its last use is now, as if a draw had made it.
+  bool PrecreateRenderTarget(RenderTargetKey key, uint64_t* host_memory_bytes_out = nullptr);
+
   // Whether depth buffer is encoded differently on the host, thus after
   // aliasing naively, precision may be lost - host depth must only be
   // overwritten if the new guest value is different than the current host depth
diff --git a/src/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.cpp b/src/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.cpp
--- a/src/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.cpp
@@ -95,6 +95,20 @@ REXCVAR_DEFINE_BOOL(d3d12_hoist_shared_memory_uploads_stats, false, "GPU/D3D12",
                     "were, every 5 seconds (with d3d12_hoist_shared_memory_uploads)")
     .lifecycle(rex::cvar::Lifecycle::kHotReload);
 
+// LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0794): the warm-up of the host allocations.
+REXCVAR_DEFINE_BOOL(d3d12_warmup, true, "GPU/D3D12",
+                    "At start, make the host allocations the first frames of a scene would make on first use (the shared "
+                    "memory's and the scaled resolve buffer's tile heaps, the host render targets), from the keys the "
+                    "earlier runs kept in <title>.rtv.d3d12.xrtp; the first run on a cache makes them on first use as "
+                    "before. Logs '[warm-up] ...'")
+    .lifecycle(rex::cvar::Lifecycle::kRequiresRestart);
+REXCVAR_DEFINE_UINT32(d3d12_warmup_mib, 0, "GPU/D3D12",
+                      "The most host memory (MiB) d3d12_warmup may allocate, spent in the order the earlier run needed the "
+                      "objects in; 0: 1024 MiB times the draw resolution scale's area, and never more than a quarter "
+                      "of the video memory the OS lets the process still have (the first 1080p front end and a drive "
+                      "of the game's first minutes need about 600 MiB at scale 1)")
+    .lifecycle(rex::cvar::Lifecycle::kRequiresRestart);
+
 REXCVAR_DECLARE(bool, gpu_regwrite_bulk);
 REXCVAR_DECLARE(bool, gpu_batch_perf_counters);
 // HDR output's trims (defined in graphics/command_processor.cpp).
@@ -479,7 +493,150 @@ void D3D12CommandProcessor::InitializeShaderStorage(const std::filesystem::path&
   // threads are done by now with a blocking preload.
   if (render_target_cache_) {
     render_target_cache_->InitializeRuntimePipelineStorage(cache_root, title_id);
+    WarmUpHostAllocations();  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0794)
+  }
+}
+
+// LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0794): see the declaration. What the earlier runs made on first use, in the order they needed it in,
+// made now within the budget, grouped by kind (the shared memory's tile heaps first, neighbours in one heap each run of
+// up to 8, then the scaled resolve buffer's, then the render targets). Nothing is guessed: a key that this run's layout
+// (the sparse granularity, the draw resolution scale) can't ask for stays in the file, unused.
+void D3D12CommandProcessor::WarmUpHostAllocations() {
+  if (!render_target_cache_ || !shared_memory_ || !texture_cache_) {
+    return;
+  }
+  std::vector<uint64_t> records = render_target_cache_->TakeWarmupRecords();
+  if (!REXCVAR_GET(d3d12_warmup)) {
+    return;
+  }
+  if (records.empty()) {
+    REXGPU_INFO("[warm-up] no host allocations stored yet in the key file: they are made on first use in this run");
+    return;
+  }
+  const auto start = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
+  const uint32_t scale_x = render_target_cache_->draw_resolution_scale_x();
+  const uint32_t scale_y = render_target_cache_->draw_resolution_scale_y();
+  uint64_t budget_bytes = REXCVAR_GET(d3d12_warmup_mib)
+                              ? uint64_t(REXCVAR_GET(d3d12_warmup_mib)) << 20
+                              : (uint64_t(1024) << 20) * scale_x * scale_y;
+  // Never more than a quarter of the video memory the OS lets the process still have.
+  bool budget_capped = false;
+  GpuMemoryInfo memory_info;
+  if (QueryGpuMemoryInfo(memory_info) && memory_info.budget_bytes) {
+    const uint64_t headroom_quarter =
+        (memory_info.budget_bytes > memory_info.usage_bytes ? memory_info.budget_bytes - memory_info.usage_bytes
+                                                            : 0) /
+        4;
+    if (headroom_quarter < budget_bytes) {
+      budget_bytes = headroom_quarter;
+      budget_capped = true;
+    }
+  }
+  const uint32_t window_log2 = shared_memory_->GetSparseAllocationGranularityLog2();
+  const uint64_t scaled_heap_bytes = D3D12TextureCache::GetScaledResolveHeapBytes();
+
+  // Choose, in the order of the file (the order the objects were first needed in), what fits the budget.
+  std::vector<uint32_t> windows, heaps, render_targets;
+  uint64_t spent = 0;
+  size_t over_budget = 0, not_for_this_run = 0;
+  for (const uint64_t record : records) {
+    const uint32_t kind = uint32_t(record >> 32);
+    const uint32_t key = uint32_t(record);
+    uint64_t bytes = 0;
+    if (kind == D3D12RenderTargetCache::kWarmupKindSharedMemoryWindow) {
+      if (window_log2 != UINT32_MAX && (key >> 24) == window_log2 &&
+          (uint64_t(key & 0xFFFFFF) << window_log2) < SharedMemory::kBufferSize) {
+        bytes = uint64_t(1) << window_log2;
+      }
+    } else if (kind == D3D12RenderTargetCache::kWarmupKindScaledResolveHeap) {
+      if (texture_cache_->IsDrawResolutionScaled() && (key >> 28) == scale_x &&
+          ((key >> 24) & 15) == scale_y) {
+        bytes = scaled_heap_bytes;
+      }
+    } else if (kind == D3D12RenderTargetCache::kWarmupKindRenderTarget) {
+      bytes = render_target_cache_->EstimateWarmupRenderTargetBytes(key);
+    }
+    if (!bytes) {
+      ++not_for_this_run;
+      continue;
+    }
+    if (spent + bytes > budget_bytes) {
+      ++over_budget;
+      continue;
+    }
+    spent += bytes;
+    if (kind == D3D12RenderTargetCache::kWarmupKindSharedMemoryWindow) {
+      windows.push_back(key & 0xFFFFFF);
+    } else if (kind == D3D12RenderTargetCache::kWarmupKindScaledResolveHeap) {
+      heaps.push_back(key & 0xFFFFFF);
+    } else {
+      render_targets.push_back(key);
+    }
+  }
+
+  using Clock = std::chrono::steady_clock;
+  auto milliseconds_since = [](Clock::time_point from) {
+    return double(std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::microseconds>(Clock::now() - from).count()) / 1000.0;
+  };
+  size_t failed = 0;
+
+  // The shared memory's tile heaps: neighbours together, a heap for each run of at most 8 windows (32 MB).
+  size_t windows_made = 0;
+  const auto windows_start = Clock::now();
+  if (!windows.empty()) {
+    std::sort(windows.begin(), windows.end());
+    windows.erase(std::unique(windows.begin(), windows.end()), windows.end());
+    for (size_t i = 0; i < windows.size();) {
+      size_t run = 1;
+      while (i + run < windows.size() && run < 8 && windows[i + run] == windows[i] + run) {
+        ++run;
+      }
+      if (shared_memory_->WarmUpHostGpuMemory(windows[i] << window_log2, uint32_t(run) << window_log2)) {
+        windows_made += run;
+      } else {
+        ++failed;
+      }
+      i += run;
+    }
   }
+  const double windows_ms = milliseconds_since(windows_start);
+
+  size_t heaps_made = 0;
+  const auto heaps_start = Clock::now();
+  for (const uint32_t heap_index : heaps) {
+    if (texture_cache_->WarmUpScaledResolveHeap(heap_index)) {
+      ++heaps_made;
+    } else {
+      ++failed;
+    }
+  }
+  const double heaps_ms = milliseconds_since(heaps_start);
+
+  size_t render_targets_made = 0;
+  uint64_t render_target_bytes = 0;
+  const auto render_targets_start = Clock::now();
+  for (const uint32_t key : render_targets) {
+    uint64_t bytes;
+    if (render_target_cache_->WarmUpRenderTarget(key, bytes)) {
+      ++render_targets_made;
+      render_target_bytes += bytes;
+    } else {
+      ++failed;
+    }
+  }
+  const double render_targets_ms = milliseconds_since(render_targets_start);
+
+  const uint64_t windows_bytes = window_log2 != UINT32_MAX ? uint64_t(windows_made) << window_log2 : 0;
+  const uint64_t heaps_bytes = uint64_t(heaps_made) * scaled_heap_bytes;
+  REXGPU_INFO(
+      "[warm-up] {} host allocations ({} MiB) made in {:.1f} ms from the key file: {} shared memory tile heap windows "
+      "({} MiB, {:.1f} ms), {} scaled resolve tile heaps ({} MiB, {:.1f} ms), {} render targets ({} MiB, {:.1f} ms); "
+      "left to the first use: {} over the {} MiB budget{}, {} that this run's layout can't ask for, {} that failed",
+      windows_made + heaps_made + render_targets_made,
+      (windows_bytes + heaps_bytes + render_target_bytes) >> 20, milliseconds_since(start), windows_made,
+      windows_bytes >> 20, windows_ms, heaps_made, heaps_bytes >> 20, heaps_ms, render_targets_made,
+      render_target_bytes >> 20, render_targets_ms, over_budget, budget_bytes >> 20,
+      budget_capped ? " (a quarter of the video memory left)" : "", not_for_this_run, failed);
 }
 
 void D3D12CommandProcessor::FlushShaderStorage(uint32_t timeout_ms) {
diff --git a/src/graphics/d3d12/render_target_cache.cpp b/src/graphics/d3d12/render_target_cache.cpp
--- a/src/graphics/d3d12/render_target_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/d3d12/render_target_cache.cpp
@@ -92,6 +92,14 @@ REXCVAR_DEFINE_STRING(render_target_path_d3d12, "", "GPU/D3D12",
 
 REXCVAR_DEFINE_BOOL(native_stencil_value_output, true, "GPU", "Enable native stencil value output");
 
+// LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0794): a first run on a cache has no key file (<title>.rtv.d3d12.xrtp), so everything it keys is
+// made on first use, with the hitches of the first frames of each scene. With this set to the path of a key file made by
+// a run on the same kind of GPU (the file's header says which: the options that change the pipelines), the new key file
+// starts as a copy of it, and the first run makes what that run made at start. The key files hold only numbers.
+REXCVAR_DEFINE_STRING(d3d12_warmup_seed, "", "GPU/D3D12",
+                      "Path of a render target key file (.xrtp) a run with no key file of its own starts from")
+    .lifecycle(rex::cvar::Lifecycle::kInitOnly);
+
 REXCVAR_DECLARE(bool, resolve_dual_write);
 REXCVAR_DECLARE(bool, resolve_dual_write_msaa);  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0530): resolve_dual_write_msaa
 // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0560): resolve_defer_memory_write (defined in resolve_defer.cpp)
@@ -2882,6 +2890,8 @@ RenderTargetCache::RenderTarget* D3D12RenderTargetCache::CreateRenderTarget(Rend
   render_target->set_host_memory_bytes(uint64_t(resource_desc.Width) * resource_desc.Height *
